    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0703" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1049</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Major General Patrick J. Hurley to Mr. Mao Tse-tung
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yenan</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-11-10">November 10, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Chairman</hi>: I am grateful to you for
                    the splendid cooperation and leadership that you have shown in bringing your
                    party to the offer of agreement which you have authorized me to take to
                    President Chiang Kai-shek and also for the splendid letter<anchor n="64"
                        xml:id="d494-f1"/> that you have given me for transmission to the President
                    of the United States.</p>
                <pb facs="0704" n="690" xml:id="pg690"/>
                <p>Be assured, Sir, that I have appreciated those qualities of mind and of heart
                    that you have brought to bear on a solution of a most difficult problem. Your
                    work is a contribution to the welfare of a United China and to the victory of
                    the United Nations.</p>
                <p>It is our earnest wish that this splendid spirit of cooperation will continue not
                    only through victory in war but through the period of making a lasting peace and
                    in the reconstruction of a democratic China.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Patrick</hi> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
